        <body>
            <div xml:id="d263">

                <pb facs="0535" n="401" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg401"/>

                <head>No. 263.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Chang Yen
                            Hoon to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-05-14"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 14, 1888</date>.
                        (Received May 14.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I had the honor to receive
                    your note of the 8th instant, informing me of the approval of the treaty by the
                    United States Senate, with two amendments, which you inclosed, written in red
                    ink on its margin, and to which I have already replied.</p>
                <p>I have the honor now to acknowledge the receipt of your note of the 11th instant,
                    inclosing a full copy of the treaty and the two amendments, and also the printed
                    copy of the treaty, with the amendments noted in red ink.</p>
                <p>I will, without delay, send them to the foreign office, which will present them,
                    with the original signed treaty, to the Throne for its decree. I will
                    communicate with you as soon as I am notified of the decree. The amendments will
                    be, in due form, noted in the certificate of exchange of ratification.</p>
                <p>I am, very truly, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chang Yen
                            Hoon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
